<title>SWEDEN: POLL-SCA H1 PROFIT SEEN UP TO 2.01 BLN SKR.</title>
<headline>POLL-SCA H1 PROFIT SEEN UP TO 2.01 BLN SKR.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish forestry group was expected to post a 20 percent rise in six-month profit after financial items to 2.01 billion crowns from 1.67 billion, a Reuter poll of 12 analysts showed on Friday.</p>
<p>Forecasts ranged from 1.78 billion to 2.09 billion crowns.</p>
<p>For the full year, analysts expect a profit of 3.91 billion crowns, which is in line with what analysts forecast ahead of SCA's first quarter report.</p>
<p>SCA is due to release six-month earnings on August 13.</p>
<p>Sources: Aros, Carnegie, CI Nordic, Den Norske Bank, Deutsche Morgan Grenfell,  Hagstromer &amp; Qviberg, Handelsbanken, James Capel, Kleinwort Benson, Matteus, Nordiska, Paribas, Salomon Brothers and Swedbank.</p>
